WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.100
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.167
is a three-time
Grammy Award-winning musician

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.234
who's celebrating
the 10th anniversary

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.133
of his mixtape "Acid Rap."

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.033
He's also a coach
on "The Voice,"

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.801
which airs Mondays
at 8:00 on NBC.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:14.601
Please welcome to the show
Chance the Rapper, everybody.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:25.267
♪♪

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:33.901
♪♪

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.300
Welcome.
I'm so happy to have you.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.000
-I'm happy to finally
be here, man.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.467
-It's a thrill for me.
This is crazy.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.868
I can't believe this has been
10 years since you put this out.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.734
Now, of course, I realize
it's only been eight years

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.167
since I was hip to it 'cause
I'm, like, a nerd, you know?

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.767
Not a nerd.
I'm, like, a loser.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:50.601
Like, I always find out about
cool music like two years later.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:51.834
So two years from now,

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.200
I'm gonna celebrate
my 10th anniversary.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.501
-That's sick, dude.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:58.968
-But this is sort of the album
that changed everything.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.901
Again, you're self-releasing it,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:03.033
so you're doing it
independently.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.767
But after this, you start
playing real big shows.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.400
-Yeah.
-Which is nuts.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.234
Did you ever -- When you're
going out and making this music

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.334
and sort of releasing it
by yourself,

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.567
did you ever think it was
gonna lead to something

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:19.033
that was not even international,
but just nationwide?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.200
-Yeah, I was like -- I was --

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.634
-Good.
Got to believe it.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:29.200
-I -- Yeah, no,
I just always wanted to --

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.300
I was always making music
and performing

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.901
and doing talent shows
since I was a little kid.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:36.200
So, like, when I decided
to become a rapper,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.033
I was always hoping
that it would be successful.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.868
I didn't really have
a plan B or anything,

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.501
but, yeah, no,
the shows just kept --

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.434
-What were the --
But what were the --

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:49.701
Like, right before you start
doing your big tour,

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.901
what were the sort of local
shows you were doing in Chicago?

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.667
Where were the venues?

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.467
-It was kind of any stage
I could get on.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:02:00.634
I played -- I played
Reggies' Rock Club

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.634
and Lincoln Hall in Chicago.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.667
I used to do shows at,
like, the --

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:09.033
at the library if I could.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.501
Man, literally anywhere.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:16.267
I performed at my aunt's breast
cancer awareness rally once.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.501
They liked it.
It was dope.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:18.868
-They did alright?
-Yeah.

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.367
-Probably a slightly
different crowd

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.834
than you were used to
at the time.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.901
Is it true that you
played a few,

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:26.033
like, high school parking lots
that had to get shut down?

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:27.901
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
No, I used to literally set up

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.200
wherever I could,
and I'd come out with, like --

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.434
I'd have posters that I'd print

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.234
with this, like,
album cover on it

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:36.000
and, like, have, like,
I don't know, T-shirts and stuff

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.634
and try and, like, sling them
in the parking lots

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.133
after school
at different high schools.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:42.834
And then, like you said,
I would get shut down.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:46.167
-Was it good for your reputation
when it would get shut down?

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.701
-Yeah, you know, actually,
that builds, like, some sort of,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.300
like, you know,
mystique around it.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.234
You got to get there
before the cops come.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.868
You know what I mean?

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.067
-I would think
that's very helpful, as well.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.567
Did you ever --
I mean, Chance the Rapper,

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:01.868
first of all, it's a great name
because it's very on the nose.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.033
-Yeah. Yeah.
-No confusion about it.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:07.834
But I have to imagine you had
some other options early on.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:13.701
-Oh, yeah, well, I had a name
when I was in eighth grade.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.300
I was --
I went by Tony Jizzle.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.167
-Okay.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.267
Maybe a wise choice
to say goodbye to Mr. Jizzle.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:25.167
-No, I'm glad that that part
of my life is over with.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:28.334
Very much so an eighth-grade
kind of name, yeah.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.968
-You're going out, you know,

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.334
sort of to celebrate
this anniversary.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:33.400
And you have a couple new shows.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.100
Can you announce
a couple new locations?

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.534
-I'm glad that we could
announce it here.

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:37.868
Yeah, so we just --

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.968
In celebration
of the 10th-year anniversary,

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.801
we put up tickets on sale
for a Chicago show

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.167
at the United Center,
and they sold out immediately.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:49.200
So by popular demand,
I decided to add two more shows,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.934
one in Los Angeles and another
one here in New York City.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:55.100
-Alright, that's fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:59.834
You had -- You mentioned
Madison Square Garden.

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:02.534
And this is -- I'm sorry, you
mentioned the United Center.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:05.033
But Madison Square Garden
once put you up on-screen.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.567
They got a little bit
of grief for this,

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.067
because if you look
at the lower third

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.234
of what they --
how they described you.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.367
Your name is Chance the Rapper.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.100
And then underneath,
they wrote "rapper."

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.467
-Yeah.

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:18.067
-And then you reached out
and you said, "In the future,

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:21.968
the titles 'Father' and 'Zaddy'
are both acceptable."

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:23.667
-Oh!
-That was nice.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.467
And now -- Then you go back.
You're at the United Center.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:31.000
And now it's your
hometown venue, right?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.834
And, I mean,
obviously they heard you.

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.033
And I think it's very nice.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.334
They put you up
Chance the Rapper, father/zaddy.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.133
[ Laughs ]

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.968
-Mid-nacho chip, too.
I'm eating.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.801
-Yeah, you never know
when they're gonna

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.534
throw you up on the screen.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:48.767
So -- And now you are a dad.
You got two girls.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.000
-I got two beautiful girls.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.701
-And that's very exciting.
How are they --

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.868
Yours are about the same ages
as mine.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.901
And I'm wondering --
I think kids are obviously

00:04:57.901 --> 00:05:02.167
maybe more drawn to music
than late-night television.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.033
Do they have any engagement
with your work?

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.467
Do they know your songs?
Do they like any of it?

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:08.767
-Yeah, they do like my music.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.667
They -- They're really --

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:14.067
They're more into, like,
Peppa Pig

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:17.334
and their contemporaries.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:18.701
Like, they're more,
like, into that.

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:22.267
But, like, I have a few songs
that they'll listen to.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.534
They like a song called
"Let's Go on the Run" a lot.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.234
-That's a good song for kids.
That's got some --

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.701
Yeah, that's a very sweet song.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.501
-I got to be careful when I'm
picking my songs for my kids.

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:31.434
But they like --

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:34.434
-Yeah, that's very funny
that I could see, you know --

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.801
I know your work enough to know

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.000
there are some songs
where you'd be like,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.868
"Do not listen
to that song by Daddy."

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:40.667
-I didn't mean this.
Yeah.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:42.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.267
I didn't mean this at all.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.968
No, yeah, no, it's cool.
But yeah.

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.501
-Would you ever think -- I mean,

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.534
in a desperate attempt
to gain their affection,

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.400
would you do a collaboration
with Peppa?

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.267
-Out of my own desperation,
I'd do a track with Peppa.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:59.567
Like, if Peppa --
if you're listening right now,

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:00.934
like, I'm trying to work

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:03.567
or at least get some autographs
for my kids.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.534
Shout-out to Peppa Pig.
-Shout-out to Peppa Pig.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:07.567
-And the Baby Shark also.
-Oh, Baby Shark.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.968
You'd work with Baby Shark?
-I would in a heartbeat.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:11.701
Is this my opportunity
to get these features?

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.901
Baby Shark.
-Any fictional characters. Yeah.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:17.100
-Thank you, man,
for giving me this spot.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.534
-I want to ask you
about "The Voice."

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:20.801
We're gonna be right back with
more from Chance the Rapper.

